{title: Father-in-Law of Midian}
{subtitle: Exodus 2:15–21; 2:21–22; 3:1–3; 18:1–12; 18:13–26; Genesis 36:4–17}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Moses fled from Pharaoh's hand
To [Bb]Midian where [C]the flocks are [Dm]kept
He [Bb]sat beside the well and saw
[F]Seven daughters drawing [C]water up
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Reuel the priest of Midian
Asked why they [Bb]came so ear[C]ly to[Dm]day
An E[Bb]gyptian rescued them he [F]said
And watered their flock that [Dm]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Moses agreed to stay with him
Who [Bb]gave his daugh[C]ter Zippo[Dm]rah
[Bb]She bore a son named [F]Gershom
In a foreign land [C]far away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]Jethro heard of God's great work
Of [Bb]Israel led [C]out of E[Dm]gypt
He [Bb]came to Moses in the [F]wild
With Zipporah [C]and their sons
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Bb]Blessed be the Lord he [Dm]cried
Who [F]rescued them from Pharaoh's [C]sword
[Bb]Now I know the Lord is [Dm]greater
Than [C]all the gods of the world
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[Dm]Moses judged the people all day
From [Bb]morning light [C]to evening [Dm]dark
His [Bb]fa-ther-in-law said to [F]him
You will wear yourself [C]out in this task
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[Dm]Look for men who fear the Lord
Trustworthy [Bb]men who [C]hate a [Dm]bribe
Ap[Bb]point them over thousands and hun[F]dreds
To judge the people [C]in their right
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
[Bb]Moses listened to his [Dm]counsel
And [F]chose capable men from Is[C]rael
[Bb]They judged the cases every [Dm]day
And went [C]home in peace and silence
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Blessed be the Lord [C]our [Dm]God
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
